  "semantics": "Goodput, replayed as capacity. bytes = bytes delivered to the application in the 100 ms bin. Continuous recording: the first warmup_s seconds (one cold start: connection setup and slow start) carry bytes with saturated = 0, and every later bin has saturated = 1. A saturated bin with bytes = 0 is a real measured zero: every connection was trying and the link delivered nothing. An EMPTY bytes field means the recorder could not measure that link in that bin (every connection was in a measurement fault such as an HTTP error status or a DNS failure, or the recorder itself stalled): missing data, never zero. Below about 1 Mbps a bin holds only a few packets, so a single zero bin can be packet timing; zero runs of 1 s or more are outages (see dropouts). A single sample of the author's own real conditions.",
